  - MIT
date-released: "2026-11-04"
keywords:
  - three-body problem
  - periodic orbits
  - linear stability
  - celestial mechanics
  - unequal masses
abstract: >-
  A one-parameter family of symmetric periodic orbits of the planar
  three-body problem (G = 1, zero angular momentum, m1 = m2 = 1, isosceles
  collinear initial conditions), free-group word ABABABAbabababaB, linearly
  stable for m3 from 4.21 to 5.034 (30-digit samples; at m3 ≈ 4.5468718 one
  index touches −2 without crossing it, a consequence of a half-period
  symmetry). Its word occurs in none of the published lists checked (Li &
  Liao 2017, Li, Jing & Liao 2018, Šuvakov & Dmitrašinović 2013, Hristov et
  al.), at any mass. At m3 = 5: a = 0.79623821011254661853007106578327, b =
  1.77433055827060488061484304997624, T =
  19.25669842976743050033657405267752, stability indices 1.47916 and
  1.43911. Includes the 30-digit data along the family, a second candidate
  (family A), and the verification code. Code and computations were written
  with Claude, an AI model by Anthropic.
